    "question_en": "Describe your understanding of MSF's core information systems (HR, supply chain, medical data, finance).",
    "answer_en": "I now see WaCA's landscape more concretely. Public WaCA recruitment material shows an active finance and ERP transition: NetSuite is being implemented for HQ general accounting, while UniField is used for field accounting; supply-chain material names Portail MSF LOG, SIRA, UniField and NetSuite P2P, including a progressive SIRA-to-UniField transition. Across the wider MSF movement, public sources also document Homere for HR/payroll, DHIS2 and tools such as Kobo/Enketo, Go.Data or EWARS for health-information and field data contexts, UniData/UniCat for trusted product master data, and Tembo for learning. I would confirm the exact WaCA production architecture, interfaces and ownership in the interview. As Systems Manager, my responsibility is not to memorize product names but to govern availability, access, lifecycle, integration, synchronization, recovery, data quality and support across them.",
    "question_ar": "صف فهمك لأنظمة المعلومات الأساسية في أطباء بلا حدود (الموارد البشرية، سلسلة الإمداد، البيانات الطبية، المالية).",
