    "question_en": "How does the AWS shared responsibility model change between EC2, RDS and Lambda?",
    "question_ar": "كيف تتغير المسؤولية المشتركة بين EC2 وRDS وLambda؟",
    "answer_en": "The boundary moves upward as the service becomes more managed. With EC2, AWS secures the facilities, hardware and virtualization layer, while I still own guest OS patching, host configuration, applications, identities, network controls and data. With RDS, AWS also manages much of the database infrastructure and platform maintenance, while I remain responsible for identities, database configuration choices, data, encryption/access policy and application behavior. With Lambda, AWS manages the servers and runtime infrastructure, but I still own the function code, IAM permissions, data handling, secrets and configuration. For an MSF Systems Manager, the practical lesson is to document the control owner per service instead of assuming “AWS handles security.”",
