    "question_ar": "متى تستخدم IAM users وroles وIdentity Center؟",
    "answer_en": "For workforce access across multiple AWS accounts, I prefer IAM Identity Center integrated with the authoritative identity source and permission sets. IAM roles provide temporary permissions for people, workloads or cross-account access and should be the default for applications rather than embedded long-lived access keys. IAM users are a narrower tool and should not be the normal pattern for a human workforce when federation/Identity Center is available. Root users are protected and reserved for the few tasks that require them. The goal is short-lived credentials, MFA, least privilege, separation of admin duties and auditable access across accounts.",
