    "question_en": "Explain the difference between high availability, backup and disaster recovery in AWS.",
    "question_ar": "ما الفرق بين HA وBackup وDR؟",
    "answer_en": "High availability keeps a service running through expected component failures, often using multiple Availability Zones, load balancing and redundant components. Backup protects recoverable copies of data and configuration. Disaster recovery is the end-to-end capability to restore or fail over the service after a major disruption within agreed RTO and RPO. They overlap but are not interchangeable: Multi-AZ does not protect against every logical deletion or ransomware scenario, and a backup that has never been restored does not prove DR. I would define failure scenarios, RTO/RPO, backup immutability/cross-account controls where justified, dependency recovery order and scheduled restore/failover tests.",
