    "question_ar": "صمم تطبيق AWS لبعثة إنترنتها ضعيف.",
    "answer_en": "I would begin with the application behavior, not the cloud service list. The field workflow should degrade gracefully: local/offline capture or queued transactions where business-safe, small payloads, resumable synchronization, explicit pending/failed states and idempotent APIs to avoid duplicates. Cloud components can use API Gateway/load balancers, queues such as SQS, durable storage and asynchronous processing, but the critical design decision is to avoid requiring a stable round trip for every user action. I would test with real latency/loss profiles, provide local contingency procedures and monitor synchronization backlog as a business metric. Cloud availability is irrelevant if the mission cannot reach the service.",
