    "question_ar": "فرّق بين CloudWatch وCloudTrail وConfig.",
    "answer_en": "CloudWatch tells me how systems are behaving through metrics, logs and alarms. CloudTrail tells me who or what made AWS API calls and changes, which is crucial for audit and incident reconstruction. AWS Config records resource configuration state and changes and can evaluate them against rules. If a database becomes publicly reachable, CloudWatch might show symptoms, CloudTrail helps identify the change action and actor, and Config helps show the configuration drift and compliance state. For the Systems Manager I want all three because observability, audit evidence and configuration governance solve different parts of the problem.",
