    "answer_en": "I would govern Azure through a landing-zone approach: management groups/subscriptions aligned to ownership and environment, policy-as-code or Azure Policy guardrails, centralized identity, network patterns, logging/monitoring, Defender/Security controls, tagging and cost management. Workloads are assessed against the five Azure Well-Architected pillars—Reliability, Security, Cost Optimization, Operational Excellence and Performance Efficiency—according to business criticality. Production and non-production should be separated, privileged access minimized, and exceptions documented. In a hybrid WaCA environment I would pay special attention to identity/network dependencies and mission connectivity. Cloud governance should make compliant deployment easier for teams; if every project needs a manual security negotiation, the platform design is not mature enough.",
