    "question_en": "How would AWS Systems Manager help you operate a fleet of EC2 servers without opening inbound admin ports?",
    "question_ar": "كيف يساعد AWS Systems Manager في تشغيل EC2؟",
    "answer_en": "Systems Manager provides operational capabilities such as inventory, Run Command, automation, patching and Session Manager for managed instances. With Session Manager, administrators can reach supported instances through an authenticated and audited control path without exposing SSH or RDP directly to the internet. I would combine that with IAM least privilege, approved maintenance workflows, patch rings, logging and change records. This is especially relevant to a Systems Manager role because the challenge is not provisioning one server; it is operating many systems consistently, remotely and audibly while reducing emergency manual access.",
