    "question_en": "What is your MDM strategy for laptops and mobile devices across multiple countries?",
    "question_ar": "ما استراتيجيتك لإدارة الأجهزة المحمولة MDM عبر عدة دول؟",
    "answer_en": "My MDM strategy starts with device personas, organizational ownership and risk. Corporate laptops and mobile devices should be inventoried and enrolled in an approved management platform such as Intune, with encryption, supported OS/patch level, screen lock, endpoint protection, configuration baselines and the ability to retire or wipe organizational data. Compliance can feed Conditional Access so unmanaged or high-risk devices do not receive the same access as compliant devices. For BYOD or constrained contexts, app-protection or limited-access patterns may be safer than full device control. I would phase enforcement and field-test policies so weak connectivity does not unintentionally lock out missions. The MSF Egypt regulations I reviewed also reinforce the basic control objective: MSF computers/phones are organizational property for authorized professional use, should be handled with care, and issues should be reported. I would confirm WaCA's exact asset-use policy while linking asset inventory, MDM, lost-device response and leaver processes.",
