    "answer_en": "I would avoid a service catalogue. I would explain the operational outcome, risks and cost. For example: “We are separating critical workloads into governed accounts, using short-lived administrator access, keeping encrypted recoverable backups outside the workload boundary, and monitoring both availability and unauthorized change. The design improves recovery and auditability for missions, but it increases recurring cloud and support costs. We will start with the critical systems, measure service availability and restore time, and review cost monthly.” Then I would state the decision required from leadership—risk appetite, RTO/RPO, budget or policy exception. The director should leave understanding the trade-off, not memorizing AWS acronyms.",
