    "answer_en": "I would treat GuardDuty as a detection signal, not the whole investigation. First I validate severity and scope, identify the affected principal, resources, region and time window, then use CloudTrail and relevant service logs to reconstruct activity. I preserve evidence before destructive changes. If credentials may be compromised, I contain through session/key revocation or permission restriction using an approved break-glass path, while avoiding actions that destroy forensic evidence. I check for persistence, data exposure and lateral movement, notify the incident owner/security function, and document the timeline. Recovery comes after containment: restore trusted configuration, rotate secrets, validate controls and capture lessons for IAM, detection and runbooks.",
