    "question_ar": "ما الفرق بين KMS وSecrets Manager وCloudHSM؟",
    "answer_en": "KMS is the default managed key-management choice for encryption keys used by many AWS services and applications. Secrets Manager stores and retrieves application secrets such as database credentials and API tokens and can support rotation workflows. CloudHSM provides dedicated hardware security modules when an organization needs direct control of HSM-backed keys or specific compliance/cryptographic requirements. I would not store a database password in KMS as though KMS were a secret vault; KMS protects cryptographic keys, while Secrets Manager manages the secret value. I would choose CloudHSM only when its control/compliance need justifies the extra operational responsibility.",
