    "answer_en": "I would avoid permanent shared credentials. The vendor gets a named, time-bound role through the approved identity path, scoped to the minimum account/resources/actions needed, with MFA where applicable and full logging. The access request states the incident, owner, start/end time and approved privileges. Where possible I use session-based managed access and screen/log recording appropriate to policy rather than opening inbound admin ports. Credentials are revoked automatically or immediately after the window, activity is reviewed, and any changes follow normal change control. This also protects MSF from vendor dependency and supports auditability and conflict-of-interest controls.",
