    "question_ar": "كيف تضمن ألا تفقد التكاملات البيانات أو تكررها دون ملاحظة؟",
    "answer_en": "I build reconciliation into the interface, not as an afterthought. Every transaction should have a stable identifier/idempotency key so retries cannot create duplicates. I track source count, accepted count, rejected count and target count, plus financial/control totals where appropriate. Failed messages go to a visible queue with reason and safe reprocessing; silent drops are unacceptable. For batch flows I use control files/hashes/totals; for APIs/events I use correlation IDs, durable logging and alerts on age/backlog. Business owners receive exception reports, particularly for finance and supply. After recovery, I reconcile end-to-end before declaring the incident closed. A green API status means very little if invoices, stock movements or master records are missing or duplicated.",
