    "question_ar": "ماذا تفعل لو Region كامل تعطل؟",
    "answer_en": "I would first activate the documented continuity plan and confirm scope: which workloads, dependencies and users are affected. Multi-AZ protects against Availability Zone failure but not a whole-Region event, so only workloads designed for cross-Region recovery can fail over. I would check recovery prerequisites—identity, DNS, network, secrets, data replication/backups and capacity—then execute the tested runbook, communicate expected RTO/RPO and reconcile data after recovery. I would not improvise a brand-new multi-Region architecture during the outage. After stabilization I would review whether the business impact justifies stronger cross-Region design for that workload.",
