    "id": 105,
    "question_en": "How would you design an AWS landing zone for MSF WaCA?",
    "question_ar": "كيف ستصمم AWS Landing Zone لـ MSF WaCA؟",
    "answer_en": "I would start with a multi-account landing zone rather than a single large account. AWS Control Tower can orchestrate a governed AWS Organizations environment with organizational units, standard account provisioning and controls. I would separate security/log archive, shared services, production, non-production and sandbox workloads according to need; centralize identity through IAM Identity Center; define SCP/control guardrails, CloudTrail/Config/log retention and mandatory tagging; and establish network/DNS and security-service patterns. Accounts and OUs should align with ownership and blast radius, not mirror the org chart unnecessarily. Before onboarding workloads I would define data classification, region constraints, RTO/RPO, support and cost allocation. The landing zone should make the secure path the easy path while allowing documented exceptions for legitimate field requirements.",
