    "question_en": "How do you give constructive feedback and feedforward to a team member?",
    "answer_en": "I prepare first, choose a private setting and the right moment, and make the purpose developmental rather than punitive. For feedback I use observable facts and the SBI structure: Situation, Behaviour, Impact. I avoid assumptions about intent and give the person space to explain. Then I move to feedforward: what should continue, what could be done differently next time, what support is needed, and what action we agree. I also adapt the delivery to the person's culture and communication style without lowering the standard. If emotions are high, I do not force the conversation at the worst moment. I confirm understanding, agree the follow-up, and document only what needs to be documented.",
