    "question_ar": "ما الفرق بين RDS Multi-AZ وRead Replica؟",
    "answer_en": "Multi-AZ is primarily an availability and failover pattern: it maintains a standby in another Availability Zone so the database can fail over when needed. A read replica is primarily for read scaling and can also support some DR patterns, but it is not the same control. I would choose Multi-AZ when availability of the transactional database matters, then add read replicas if the workload has significant read demand or a separate reporting need. I would still test application reconnect behavior and restores, because a managed database feature does not automatically prove end-to-end continuity.",
