    "answer_en": "I would not treat a manager request as sufficient authorization for sensitive health information. I would verify the applicable WaCA/mission policy and use the designated confidential channel. The Egypt regulations give a useful principle: medical certificates are handled through the staff-health focal point rather than distributed to the line manager or HR, specifically to protect medical confidentiality. Technically, I would minimize recipients, use approved secure storage/sharing, avoid unnecessary copies, and make sure access is auditable. If the operational team only needs absence status, they should receive that status rather than the medical detail.",
