    "question_en": "How would you use upward and peer feedback as a manager?",
    "answer_en": "I would make it safe, structured and useful. I would invite input from the people who work closely with me or the employee, explain why the feedback is being collected, and protect confidentiality. I would look for recurring themes rather than forwarding raw comments or trying to identify who said what. I would give equal weight to recognition and corrective themes, discuss two or three actionable points, and convert them into development actions. I also need to model how to receive feedback: listen, clarify, avoid defensiveness, reflect before rejecting it, and thank the person for taking the risk to speak. The OCB material I reviewed makes upward feedback compulsory for managerial roles in that process; I would verify WaCA's exact mechanism.",
