    "question_ar": "اكتشف Macie بيانات حساسة في S3 bucket لا يجب أن تحتويها. ماذا تفعل؟",
    "answer_en": "I first confirm the finding and business owner, then assess whether the data is merely present or also exposed. I check bucket policy, public access settings, IAM access, object encryption and CloudTrail/S3 access evidence. I contain inappropriate access without deleting evidence, notify the data owner/privacy-security chain, and decide whether the object should be quarantined, reclassified, moved or deleted under retention policy. Then I fix the root cause: upload workflow, classification, data minimization, guardrails and alerting. Macie helps discover sensitive data in S3; it does not by itself enforce the full remediation workflow.",
