    "question_en": "What steps do you take to protect sensitive data against breaches?",
    "answer_en": "I use defence in depth across the data lifecycle: minimize and classify data, enforce strong identity and least privilege, encrypt in transit and at rest, secure endpoints with MDM/EDR, segment networks, harden and patch systems, protect secrets, log privileged and sensitive actions, and maintain tested backups. I also control the ways data leaves the organization—integrations, exports, email, vendors, removable media and social platforms. The MSF Egypt regulations I reviewed add a very practical rule: confidential information is for authorized official purposes and need-to-know access only, with no unnecessary copying or sharing. For humanitarian data, I also assess physical and reputational harm if information is exposed, not only regulatory impact.",
