    "question_ar": "كيف تختار S3 storage class؟",
    "answer_en": "I would start from access frequency, retrieval-time requirement, minimum storage duration, resilience requirement and predictability of the access pattern. S3 Standard fits frequent access; Intelligent-Tiering is useful when access is changing or unknown; infrequent-access classes trade lower storage cost for retrieval and minimum-duration considerations; Glacier classes are for archive with different retrieval characteristics. A lifecycle policy can transition or expire objects based on governance and retention rules. For MSF I would never optimize cost by moving operationally critical data into a tier whose restore time violates the RTO, and I would keep deletion/retention aligned with data-protection rules.",
