    "question_en": "Differentiate Amazon Inspector, Systems Manager Patch Manager and Security Hub in one vulnerability case.",
    "question_ar": "فرّق بين Amazon Inspector وSystems Manager Patch Manager وSecurity Hub في حالة vulnerability واحدة.",
    "answer_en": "Inspector identifies and prioritizes relevant vulnerability/exposure findings for supported workloads. Systems Manager Patch Manager is an operational control to orchestrate patching against approved baselines and maintenance windows. Security Hub aggregates and correlates security findings/posture across services so the security team can prioritize centrally. In a real workflow I would detect and assess with Inspector, decide the remediation window based on risk and availability, patch through Systems Manager where appropriate, and track the security finding through the organization's central process. None of those replaces application testing, asset ownership or change control.",
