    "answer_en": "I would use account structure for strong ownership boundaries where practical, then enforce a tagging taxonomy for cost center/project/environment/owner and activate the relevant cost-allocation tags. AWS Organizations provides consolidated billing across member accounts, while Cost Explorer and detailed cost-and-usage data can report by linked account, service and tags. Shared-service costs need an agreed allocation rule rather than disappearing into “IT overhead.” I would publish a monthly showback dashboard, investigate unowned spend and connect architectural decisions to unit cost. Cost governance should make service owners accountable without encouraging unsafe cost cutting.",
