    "question_en": "How do you collaborate cross-functionally with logistics, medical, HR, and finance departments on IS needs?",
    "answer_en": "I use service and process ownership to connect functions. Medical, Supply, HR and Finance own the business outcomes and rules; Information Systems owns technical service health, architecture, lifecycle, integration and supportability; Security/DPO define controls; Support handles user-facing operations; vendors provide contracted expertise. For a change such as ERP integration, I would run joint discovery around business events and data owners, document interfaces and decision rights, agree UAT and cutover criteria, and keep a single RAID/decision log. This avoids the common failure where each department optimizes its part but no one owns the end-to-end flow. Success is measured on the business transaction completing correctly across systems, not on individual applications being 'green'.",
