    "answer_en": "I manage an enterprise application from demand through retirement. Before acquisition: business owner, requirements, security/privacy, architecture, integration, support and exit criteria. During implementation: environments, data migration, testing/UAT, access roles, documentation, monitoring, backup/recovery, support model and operational acceptance. In service: availability, incidents/problems, releases, vulnerabilities, licence/vendor performance, access reviews, capacity, data quality and user adoption. Lifecycle reviews identify vendor EOL, obsolete customizations and replacement options early. Retirement includes data retention/export, integration shutdown, credential revocation, licence termination and evidence that no hidden dependency remains. The business owner remains accountable for process and value; Systems owns technical health and supportability.",
