    "answer_en": "CloudFormation is infrastructure as code: define and version AWS resources so environments are reproducible and changes are reviewable. Elastic Beanstalk is a higher-level application deployment platform that provisions and manages common infrastructure for supported application stacks. Systems Manager is for ongoing fleet/operations management such as inventory, automation, remote administration and patch orchestration. I might use all three in one environment: CloudFormation for the baseline, Beanstalk for an application platform, and Systems Manager for operations. The key is lifecycle separation: provision, deploy, operate.",
