    "answer_en": "I treat a major upgrade as a business change with technical controls. Start with vendor support/EOL reason, dependency and compatibility assessment, data/integration impacts and a tested rollback strategy. Build a representative non-production environment, execute regression/security/performance tests and business UAT, rehearse migration/cutover, and freeze unrelated changes. Communicate impact by user group, train only what changes and staff hypercare with clear escalation. For integrations, confirm both endpoints and reconciliation after cutover. Backups and recovery are verified before the change, not assumed. I use explicit go/no-go criteria and business-owner sign-off. If field connectivity could affect deployment, stage content and plan waves rather than force a simultaneous global upgrade.",
