    "answer_en": "I translate neutrality, impartiality and independence into technology decisions, not just values statements. I would collect only data needed for legitimate medical or operational purposes, restrict access by role, avoid unnecessary disclosure to external actors, and assess whether a system, hosting location or integration could expose patients, staff or operations to physical or political risk. Independence also means avoiding preventable technical lock-in and maintaining export, continuity and exit options. When a request creates tension between operational convenience and humanitarian risk, I would involve the appropriate medical, data-protection, security and operational owners, document the decision, and choose the option that protects people and preserves MSF's ability to act independently.",
