    "question_en": "How do you manage business continuity and disaster recovery planning for critical systems?",
    "answer_en": "I separate high availability, backup and disaster recovery because they solve different failures. First, a business impact analysis defines critical services, dependencies, RTO and RPO. Then I design redundancy for expected component failures, protected backups for corruption/ransomware/deletion, and a DR strategy for site, region or identity-service failure. Each service needs an owner, dependency map, runbook, communication path and recovery priority. Backups are not evidence until restores are tested. I would run tabletop exercises plus scheduled technical restore/failover tests, record actual recovery time and data loss, and track gaps to closure. For field systems, the plan must also cover long connectivity loss and local continuation of essential work.",
    "question_ar": "كيف تدير التخطيط لاستمرارية الأعمال والتعافي من الكوارث للأنظمة الحرجة؟",
