    "answer_en": "The defining challenge is heterogeneity. One mission may have stable office connectivity while another depends on satellite links, intermittent power or limited local technical capacity. At the same time, finance, supply, HR and medical reporting still need reliable data, controlled access and organizational oversight. I would design for graceful degradation: local or offline operation where the business process requires it, resumable synchronization, bandwidth-aware updates, simple recovery, local ownership and strong central observability. I would also avoid assuming that every MSF operational directorate or mission has the same application stack. The governance model should standardize non-negotiables—identity, security, data protection, backup, integration and support—while allowing implementation patterns that fit the mission context.",
