    "answer_en": "I would structure incident response around NIST CSF 2.0 and the current NIST SP 800-61 Rev. 3 principles. Preparation means ownership, logging, contact paths, backups and exercises. During an incident: detect and validate, classify severity and humanitarian impact, contain without destroying evidence, eradicate the cause, recover from trusted states and monitor for recurrence. Communications, legal/DPO/security and operational leadership are engaged according to impact. For sensitive MSF data I would consider whether notification itself creates risk. Afterward I want a blameless review, root cause, control improvements and tracked actions. The measure of maturity is not whether incidents happen; it is whether we detect, contain and recover with controlled impact.",
