    "answer_en": "I use identity as the primary control plane: one authoritative joiner–mover–leaver process, unique accounts, strong MFA, least privilege, role/group-based access, Conditional Access, device context where appropriate, privileged access management and regular access reviews. Administrative identities should be separate from daily accounts and high privilege should be just-in-time where the platform supports it. Service identities need owners, scoped permissions, rotation and secrets management. For remote missions I would test resilience to federation or connectivity failure and maintain tightly controlled emergency access. The key governance link is HR: role changes and departures must reliably trigger access changes, while application owners remain accountable for approving business permissions.",
