    "question_en": "How do you approach network design connecting HQ to field offices/missions (hub-and-spoke model)?",
    "answer_en": "I would avoid assuming that 'hub-and-spoke' means all traffic must hairpin through HQ. I start with application location, identity, security inspection, latency, bandwidth, offline requirements and failure modes. Stable sites may use SD-WAN/VPN patterns with redundant internet; remote projects may need satellite or cellular alternatives and bandwidth prioritization. Cloud/SaaS access may be better served by controlled local breakout when security architecture allows it. I would segment networks, separate administrative access, centralize logging where feasible, monitor link quality and define failover paths for critical services. The design should degrade safely: when the WAN is unavailable, the mission should know exactly which functions continue locally and how queued data will synchronize later.",
