    "question_en": "Describe your approach to integrating disparate legacy systems.",
    "answer_en": "I start by mapping the systems, owners, interfaces, data entities and business events—not by connecting databases directly. I identify an authoritative source for each master entity, define stable identifiers and data contracts, then choose an integration pattern: API, event/queue, batch or managed file exchange based on latency and reliability needs. Interfaces need authentication, least privilege, encryption, retries, idempotency, error queues, observability and reconciliation. I would introduce an anti-corruption/canonical layer where legacy semantics differ rather than spread old inconsistencies into new systems. Migration should be incremental, with parallel validation and a retirement plan for obsolete interfaces so integration work actually reduces rather than increases technical debt.",
