    "question_en": "How do you manage IT asset lifecycle across multiple country offices?",
    "answer_en": "I manage assets as a lifecycle from request to secure disposal. Each device should have an owner, location, serial/asset identity, configuration baseline, support/warranty status, encryption and MDM status, software/licence assignment and end-of-life date. Procurement and standard builds reduce variation; MDM/endpoint tools provide compliance and remote actions; local stock and spares are sized for field lead times. Transfers between staff or countries must update custody records, and leavers trigger retrieval/wipe. Disposal must include verified data sanitization and evidence, especially for devices that may contain sensitive information. I would report exceptions such as unsupported OS, missing encryption, inactive devices and warranty/EOL risk rather than treating inventory as a once-a-year spreadsheet.",
