    "question_en": "What governance frameworks (ITIL, COBIT, TOGAF) do you use, and how have you applied them?",
    "answer_en": "I use frameworks as toolboxes, not as bureaucracy. ITIL-aligned practices are useful for service ownership, incidents, problems, changes, requests, SLAs and continual improvement. COBIT helps at the governance layer—decision rights, accountability, controls and assurance. TOGAF helps structure architecture baselines, target states, roadmaps and governance for complex change. I also use NIST CSF 2.0 for cybersecurity risk and ISO 22301 concepts for business continuity. I would not try to 'implement a framework' everywhere. For WaCA I would select the practices that solve real problems—for example service ownership and change control for enterprise applications, architecture review for NetSuite/integrations, and measurable recovery testing for critical services.",
