    "answer_en": "I would define the minimum operational outcome first, then protect the non-negotiables: security, data protection, continuity and supportability. I would rank requirements as must/should/could, design for low bandwidth and simple local support, reuse shared MSF capabilities where appropriate, and prefer phased deployment to a large one-time build. Total cost must include licences, connectivity, devices, training, support, integration and exit—not only implementation. I would pilot with a representative mission, capture evidence, and scale only what works. Limited budget is not a reason to accept uncontrolled technical debt; it is a reason to make the trade-offs explicit and focus resources on the highest mission impact and risk reduction.",
