    "answer_en": "I negotiate from requirements, integrity and exit risk—not only price. Before negotiation I define service criticality, support hours, response/resolution targets, security and data obligations, implementation responsibilities, acceptance criteria and expected volume. I then negotiate measurable SLAs, escalation, renewal and licence terms, data ownership/export, breach notification, audit rights, subprocessors, BCP/DR, change/EOL notice, knowledge transfer and termination assistance. I also keep procurement integrity explicit: any actual or perceived conflict of interest must be declared and managed, and gifts or favours from a supplier should never influence a decision. After signature, contract governance continues through service reviews, access reviews, risk tracking and renewal decisions.",
