    "answer_en": "In a humanitarian organization, value is not best expressed as financial ROI alone. I would measure whether systems help teams deliver operations safely and reliably: availability of critical services, user-impact minutes, MTTR, successful recovery tests, security exposure, access-review completion, integration errors, data-quality exceptions, lifecycle risk, adoption and support burden. For major investments I would also track avoided manual work, reduced duplicate data entry, faster month-end or supply processing, and improved auditability. I would combine those indicators with qualitative feedback from missions and functional owners. The question is: did the investment improve mission capability or reduce material risk at a sustainable total cost, not simply did it reduce IT spending?",
