    "question_en": "How do you evaluate whether to build custom systems in-house vs buy off-the-shelf?",
    "answer_en": "I compare build, buy and configure based on strategic differentiation, functional fit, security, integration, offline needs, time-to-value, internal skills, total cost, lifecycle and exit risk. If the requirement is a common enterprise process—finance, HR, identity or ITSM—I normally prefer a mature product/configuration unless there is a compelling gap. Custom development makes sense when the workflow is genuinely distinctive, integrations are manageable and we can fund long-term ownership. I avoid both extremes: forcing a package into an unsafe workflow and building a bespoke system just because we can. A proof of concept and five-year TCO/support model usually expose the real trade-off.",
