    "answer_en": "I favor a pragmatic hybrid. Infrastructure, ERP migration and regulated changes often need clear scope, architecture, dependencies, cutover and approval gates; application and integration work benefits from short iterations, demos and rapid feedback. I therefore use Agile practices inside a governance envelope: product/backlog ownership, iterative delivery and retrospectives, combined with RAID management, architecture/security checkpoints, test/UAT evidence, change control and production-readiness criteria. Methodology should fit risk and uncertainty. In a humanitarian environment I also keep the process lightweight enough that it does not delay urgent operations, while preserving the controls needed to prevent unsafe changes to critical systems.",
