    "question_en": "How do you build and manage an annual IT budget for a multi-country operation?",
    "answer_en": "I would build the budget from the service portfolio and roadmap. Baseline recurring commitments—licences, support, connectivity, hosting/cloud, warranties and essential staffing—then add lifecycle replacements, security/continuity gaps and approved projects. Costs should be mapped to service/business owners and categorized as run, protect, improve and transform so leadership can see what is discretionary. I would include multi-year commitments, exchange-rate or country uncertainty, vendor renewal dates and contingency for critical field needs. During the year I would forecast actual versus budget, monitor cloud/licence consumption and re-prioritize based on risk and mission demand. Cutting cost should not silently remove recovery capacity or security controls; trade-offs need explicit ownership.",
